course: dictionary
lesson: 2634
title: Dessert: the sweet end of the meal
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dessert is the sweet food eaten at the end of a meal, like ice cream, pudding, fruit or cake. The words around it give you clues. «For dessert, we had ice cream» tells you that dessert comes after the main meal.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «After the main course, we had pudding.» Pudding fits, so dessert means the sweet food at the end. You will also see phrases like «dessert spoon» and «dessert menu».
explain: Be careful with food words. Some sound like desserts but are not. Kompot is sweet, but it is a drink. Context and a dictionary will tell you which is which.
fact: Dessert is the sweet food eaten at the end of a meal.
fact: Dessert usually comes after the main course, but in France «le fromage» (cheese) often comes before dessert.
fact: Kompot is a drink, not a dessert, even though it is sweet.
fact: Syrniki are made with soft cottage cheese, not cheddar, and holubtsi means «little doves» but has no birds inside.
fact: People in Tang China, Persia and Arab lands made frozen sweets long ago, so ice cream has several early homes and no clear first.
exercise: «For dessert, we had ice cream.» What is dessert in this sentence? | The main meal of the day | *The sweet food at the end of the meal | A kind of drink | A small spoon for soup
exercise: Is kompot a dessert? | *No, it is a drink | Yes, it is always eaten at the end of a meal | Yes, because it is sweet
exercise: «A pie was cut into 4 equal pieces for dessert.» What fraction is one piece? | 4/1 | *1/4 | 3/4 | 1/2
test: «Mum skipped dessert because she was being good.» What does skipped mean here? | Ate it twice | Hid it under the table | *Did not eat it | Bought it for everyone
test: Which word means the sweet food at the end of a meal? | Main course | *Pudding | Kompot | Cheddar
exam: Which of these is a dessert? | *Ice cream | Bread | Salad | Soup
